  "details": "crash on fbt calibration if shoulder rotator component already present on avatar root.\nShoulder rotator makes the IK solver update twice but it's in a bit of an error prone way.\nIt goes IKSolver.Update, which calls OnPostUpdate. ShoulderRotator.Update is registered as a callback on the OnPostUpdate event.\nShoulderRotator.Update calls IKSolver.Update again after its update which would lead to infinite recursion but ShoulderRotator keeps track of whether it's already updated each frame and just returns the second time it's called. Apparently having two ShoulderRotators makes it bounce back-and-forth forever.\nSolution: check if the component already exists in the avatar validation step.",
